{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1526","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Mean Inequality"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of $$$2n$$$ "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"distinct"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" integers. You want to arrange the elements of the array in a circle such that no element is equal to the the arithmetic mean of its $$$2$$$ neighbours."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"More formally, find an array $$$b$$$, such that: "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$b$$$ is a permutation of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For every $$$i$$$ from $$$1$$$ to $$$2n$$$, $$$b_i \\neq \\frac{b_{i-1}+b_{i+1}}{2}$$$, where $$$b_0 = b_{2n}$$$ and $$$b_{2n+1} = b_1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proved that under the constraints of this problem, such array $$$b$$$ always exists."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input contains a single integer $$$t$$$ $$$(1 \\leq t \\leq 1000)$$$ — the number of testcases. The description of testcases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each testcase contains a single integer $$$n$$$ $$$(1 \\leq n \\leq 25)$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each testcase contains $$$2n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_{2n}$$$ $$$(1 \\leq a_i \\leq 10^9)$$$ — elements of the array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that there is no limit to the sum of $$$n$$$ over all testcases."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each testcase, you should output $$$2n$$$ integers, $$$b_1, b_2, \\ldots b_{2n}$$$, for which the conditions from the statement are satisfied."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3\n3\n1 2 3 4 5 6\n2\n123 456 789 10\n1\n6 9\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n3 1 4 2 5 6\n123 10 456 789\n9 6\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first testcase, array $$$[3, 1, 4, 2, 5, 6]$$$ works, as it's a permutation of $$$[1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]$$$, and $$$\\frac{3+4}{2}\\neq 1$$$, $$$\\frac{1+2}{2}\\neq 4$$$, $$$\\frac{4+5}{2}\\neq 2$$$, $$$\\frac{2+6}{2}\\neq 5$$$, $$$\\frac{5+3}{2}\\neq 6$$$, $$$\\frac{6+1}{2}\\neq 3$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1526A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1526/problem/A"}